{
  "id": "ss.char.donut",
  "name": "Donut",
  "description": "A survivor built around a hole. The shell closed into a ring where the emitter chamber used to be, so this one did not just go quiet — it grew over the wound, and you can see the ground through where its chest should be. The torso is that ring, coral plate around nothing, with the shoulders on a yoke above it and the dead organ set on the rim off to one side, the way it always was. A row of husk spines runs off the far shoulder, and in the near hand it holds three wing blades fanned like a hand of cards: Drifter membranes on bone frames, thrown to bounce from body to body. That fan is the tell for the luck it runs on, and the pouch on the belt is the jelly it hoards. Same feelers as the rest; bare chitin cold slate, coral plate over it. Drawn facing +x; the game flips it.",
